// title: Who signs in with the device code flow, by user and application, last 30 days
// date: 2026-11-18
// product: Entra
// tables: SigninLogs
// purpose: Successful and failed sign-ins whose AuthenticationProtocol is deviceCode, grouped by user and application, with the IP addresses and countries seen. Complements the 12 September query (device code followed by a new security-info registration), which hunts the attack; this one scopes the block. Not 
// source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/reference/tables/signinlogs
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l)
// Microsoft SOC Brief 18 Nov 2026 - device code flow use, to scope a Conditional Access block
// Columns as on the SigninLogs reference cited beside this query. Not run against a tenant in this pass.
SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(30d)
| where AuthenticationProtocol == "deviceCode"
| summarize SignIns = count(), Failures = countif(ResultType != "0"), IPs = make_set(IPAddress, 20),
            Countries = make_set(tostring(LocationDetails.countryOrRegion), 10), First = min(TimeGenerated), Last = max(TimeGenerated)
          by UserPrincipalName, AppDisplayName, AppId
| sort by SignIns desc
